# Drafted, not run: no host has loaded, enabled or started this unit (the worktree that authored it made no host
# changes). stack-currency.service pulls it in (Wants=) and orders itself after it (After=), so the daily
# stack-currency.timer runs the watch first and scripts/currency_due.py then counts its fresh latest.json. It has no
# [Install] section and no timer of its own, matching this directory's timer-triggered oneshot convention.
#
# Wants= is the weak dependency of systemd.unit(5) (systemd 255.4-1ubuntu8.17 on the workstation): "if the listed
# units fail to start or cannot be added to the transaction, this has no impact on the validity of the transaction
# as a whole, and this unit will still be started". For a service, After= waits until "all its configured start-up
# commands have been invoked and they either failed or reported start-up success" (the same page), so a failed,
# timed-out or missing watch never blocks the currency run. currency_due.py then counts the last report whose data is
# at most three days old (a source the watch took from the cache after a failed fetch keeps its fetch time); an older,
# future-dated or unreadable report is "surface watch stale" or "surface watch unreadable", a check that could not
# answer (the earlier notice stays and the line never says "nothing due"), and no report is the coverage note "surface
# watch not run".
#
# @REPOSITORY@ is the live clone, as for stack-currency.service (never the working checkout or a build worktree).
# Install both services and the timer together and verify them (adoption/lifecycle.md):
#   sed 's#@REPOSITORY@#%h/code/native-agent-stack-live#g' adoption/templates/systemd/upstream-surface-watch.service > ~/.config/systemd/user/upstream-surface-watch.service
#   systemd-analyze --user verify ~/.config/systemd/user/upstream-surface-watch.service ~/.config/systemd/user/stack-currency.service ~/.config/systemd/user/stack-currency.timer
#
# The run fetches public sources (npm registry, unpkg, code.claude.com, raw.githubusercontent.com, GitHub release
# downloads) and makes `gh api` calls with gh's own stored sign-in; it makes no model call, reads no credential and
# writes only ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/native-agent-stack/surface-watch/ (cache/ and latest.json, mode
# 0600). It runs `codex features list` with an empty temporary HOME and CODEX_HOME, so the host's Codex home is
# neither read nor written. PATH holds the ecosystem bin directory for gh and codex, as in stack-currency.service.
# TimeoutStartSec= bounds the whole run (each fetch is bounded at 60 s). docs/upstream-surface-watch.md.
[Unit]
Description=Write the upstream-surface watch report for the currency notice (public fetches, no model call)

[Service]
Type=oneshot
UMask=0077
NoNewPrivileges=true
Nice=10
IOSchedulingClass=best-effort
IOSchedulingPriority=7
TimeoutStartSec=600
Environment=PATH=%h/.local/share/codex-ecosystem/bin:%h/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
Environment=PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
ExecStart=/usr/bin/python3 @REPOSITORY@/scripts/upstream_surface_watch.py --network
